bc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"## Investigation (read-only, 2026-11-18 PST)\n\nWhich pass created REB-7141: the hourly Reconcile Bridge run 43237101698 (scheduled 2026-11-12 14:25:53Z, live profile, nava-rebar 0.15.1 built from main). Evidence:\n- Jira `created`: REB-7141 at 14:34:25.536Z, REB-7142 at 14:34:45.249Z, 19.7 s apart. Both have creator Joe Oakhart (the bridge's Jira user) and the same summary.\n- `refs/reconciler/lock` history: the only holder between 13:32Z and 15:28Z is that run (lock commits 14:30:24Z to 14:37:23Z). No other pass, canary or MCP bridge op held the lock. The heartbeat canary (14:05Z) does not create Jira issues.\n- The run's log shows `RECON: outbound_differ total=29 create=1`, no error lines, and `BRIDGE_STATE: converged`. So the pass issued ONE create mutation and two Jira issues resulted inside it.\n- The pending binding was written at 14:33:41Z (write-ahead), then REB-7142 was recorded. REB-7141 never got the `rebar-id:b23c-\u2026` label, so the next pass (15:25Z) imported it as `jira-reb-7141`.\n\nWhy the key was not recorded: the coordinator calls `client.create_issue` once (`create_route._CoordinatedSeams.create_execute`), but the Cloud transport retries inside that call. `acli_subprocess._run_acli` loops up to `_MAX_ATTEMPTS = 3` and retries ANY non-zero ACLI exit except auth and assignee errors, with a 2 s backoff, including `jira workitem create` (lines ~555-565). It logs nothing on a retried attempt and prints stderr only when every attempt fails, which matches the silent log. A create that landed in Jira but exited non-zero is re-run, and the second issue is the one whose key is returned and bound. A second in-transport re-create exists for assignee errors (`_create_from_json_payload` returns None, then the caller re-creates without the assignee); the ticket had priority 2, so the create went through `_create_issue_from_json`.\n\nNot established: which of those two retry branches fired (the transport logs neither) and the ACLI exit status of the first attempt.\n\nRelation to 21fc: that fix covers index lag in recovery and dedup. It does not touch the transport's own retry loop, so it does not cover this path. RP-03 S4 T1 (`colloquial-key-groundhog`) required \"one physical create invocation issues exactly one provider create call\"; the ACLI transport loop still violates that on Cloud.","timestamp":1795068633999974843},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implementation: commit 4a8caf04479 (local worktree c2-cloud-create-once), waiting for a make verify slot.\n- RED reproduced: `_run_acli` ran `jira workitem create` 3 times after a non-zero exit, and a lost-response create followed by a second pass made 2 issues.\n- Fix: `_NON_REPLAYABLE_COMMANDS` in acli_subprocess stops replay of a create (a 429 still retries). `_CoordinatedSeams.create_payload` adds `rebar-id:<local_id>` to the create payload, and the Cloud create forwards it (`--label` / JSON `labels`).\n- Tests: `tests/unit/reconciler/test_cloud_create_single_attempt.py` (6 tests, including the end-to-end lost-response case, which now ends with 1 issue bound by `dedup-create-skipped`). `pytest tests/unit/reconciler tests/scripts`: 5,517 passed, 2 skipped.\n- Unverified: a live Cloud create with `--label`. The flag is in `acli jira workitem create --help` (ACLI 1.3.19 on this Mac), but no live issue was created to test it.\n- Not changed: the existing duplicate REB-7141 / `jira-reb-7141`. Both Jira issues are Done; cleaning them up is a separate data action.","timestamp":1795073095124554009},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Landed: Gerrit 3452 merged as fa383b1d195a5795271f56baa1fbdb17fcd69f21. Patch set 1 got LLM-Review -1: no test covered the label forwarding in `AcliClient.create_issue`. Patch set 2 adds that test (it fails when the forwarding is removed). It also stops typed-path label-operation dicts from being stringified into Jira labels, now that only plain-string labels plus the identity label are sent, and adds tests for the merge and no-duplicate branches. Patch set 2: LLM-Review +1, Verified +1 (run 44529616374). Local make verify passed on 47bbe3b0452: 21,461 passed plus 226 integration.\nFollow-up filed: `oppressed-topsecret-chickadee` (DC create replay on connection faults; ACLI comment create replay). Windows sweep dispatched: run 44534782876.","timestamp":1795095439145506545}],"created_at":1795027404944041501,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"6d4d1d76-e0d0-46be-b6ee-afbb7fbc28d9","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"jira-reb-7141"},{"link_uuid":"3784b317-0a6b-4bf0-9547-8b9ca15cfb14","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"b342-c10c-14b4-4185"},{"link_uuid":"7c27c9a8-8527-4dfa-83e4-55fd11fc4d99","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"eb07-47d5-f8f5-49f3"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nOne outbound create for `sweating-revolting-oriole` (b23c-8220-e09f-448a) produced two Jira Cloud issues. REB-7142 was bound; REB-7141 got no identity label, so the next pass imported it as a duplicate ticket `jira-reb-7141`. Any Cloud create that lands in Jira but whose ACLI call exits non-zero can do the same.\n\n### Observation (read-only, 2026-11-18 PST)\n- REB-7141 created 2026-11-12 14:34:25.536Z and REB-7142 at 14:34:45.249Z, same summary, same creator. Both inside Reconcile Bridge run 43237101698, the only `refs/reconciler/lock` holder from 13:32Z to 15:28Z. That run logged `outbound_differ ... create=1` and no error. Details: comment of 2026-11-18 on this ticket.\n- The coordinator calls `client.create_issue` once (`src/rebar/reconciler/create_route.py:249`, `_CoordinatedSeams.create_execute`), but the Cloud transport re-runs the call: `acli_subprocess._run_acli` (`src/rebar/reconciler/adapters/jira/acli_subprocess.py:472`) retries any non-zero ACLI exit except auth and assignee errors up to `_MAX_ATTEMPTS = 3`, including `jira workitem create`, and logs nothing on a retried attempt. Its own docstring already says timed-out writes are not retried \"because a server-side write may already have landed\"; a non-zero exit after the write landed is the same case.\n- The Cloud create sends no identity label (`acli_cli_ops._create_issue_no_json` at :216, `_create_issue_from_json` at :306); the `rebar-id:` label is added after the key comes back. So when the response is lost, label-based recovery (`create_route` `observe` at :265, `binding_recovery.recover_pending_bindings`) cannot find the landed issue, and after the grace window the create is issued again.\n- Closed bug `21fc-51d7-90ca-4a03` fixed index lag in recovery and dedup; it does not touch the transport loop. RP-03 S4 T1 (`colloquial-key-groundhog`) required \"one physical create invocation issues exactly one provider create call\", which this loop violates on Cloud.\n\n## Approach\nTwo changes; together a create whose response is lost cannot become a second issue.\n1. No in-transport replay of a create. `_run_acli` decides by command shape, the way `_check_mutation_failure` already inspects the command: for `jira workitem create` (a new module constant `_NON_REPLAYABLE_COMMANDS`), a non-zero exit raises at once unless `_rate_limit_backoff` detects a 429, which Jira rejects without applying, so that retry stays. No new parameter, so the test fakes that replace `_run_acli` with a fixed signature (`tests/unit/reconciler/test_operation_bindings_runtime.py:164`, `tests/scripts/conftest.py` `acli_capture`, `tests/unit/reconciler/state/test_acli_subprocess_timeout.py` `record_run`) keep working unchanged. No config key, env var or flag.\n2. Identity label at create. `_CoordinatedSeams.create_execute` adds `labels: [\"rebar-id:<local_id>\"]` to the payload it hands `create_issue` (create mutations carry labels separately, in `mutation.labels`, not in `fields`, per `outbound_mutation_builders._compute_outbound_create_mutation`). The Cloud create maps `labels` to `--label` (no-JSON path) and the JSON `labels` array (`--from-json`, which `acli jira workitem create --generate-json` lists). DC already passes unknown create fields through to Jira (`_translate_create_fields`, `jira_datacenter/_issues.py:86`), so `labels` reaches the DC REST create too. The later `attach_label` step re-adds the same label, which is idempotent.\nA landed-but-failed create then fails the mutation with its pending binding kept, and the next pass's label observation or recovery binds the existing issue instead of creating another.\nPortability: no process, signal, path or encoding change; only arguments to the existing ACLI invocation.\n\n## Scope\n- `src/rebar/reconciler/adapters/jira/acli_subprocess.py`: no replay of a non-zero create.\n- `src/rebar/reconciler/adapters/jira/acli_cli_ops.py`: labels at create.\n- `src/rebar/reconciler/adapters/jira/acli.py`: forward `labels` from the payload.\n- `src/rebar/reconciler/create_route.py`: identity label in the create payload.\n- `tests/unit/reconciler/test_cloud_create_single_attempt.py` (new).\n- `tests/unit/reconciler/orchestrate/test_leaves_effect_matrix.py`: its exact create-payload assertion (:143) now expects the added `labels` entry. The other payload checks (`tests/unit/reconciler/apply/test_applier.py:230`, `tests/unit/reconciler/apply/test_applier_dedup.py:178`) read single keys and are unaffected.\n\n## Testing\n- Dropped response: a fake ACLI records each create (with its labels) in a state file and exits non-zero on the first create. One coordinated create plus a following recovery pass leaves exactly one recorded issue, carrying `rebar-id:<local_id>`, and the binding resolves to its key.\n- A 429 on create is still retried and succeeds with one issue.\n- Non-create commands keep their retries (existing `tests/unit/reconciler/state/test_acli_auth_failure.py::test_non_auth_failure_still_retries_the_full_budget` stays green).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] The pass that created REB-7141 and the reason its key was not recorded are identified from the run log, lock history and Jira timestamps (recorded in the 2026-11-18 comment).\n- [x] The Cloud create path is fixed, with a regression test that drops the create response and asserts one issue results; `pytest tests/unit/reconciler/test_cloud_create_single_attempt.py` passes.\n- [x] `pytest tests/unit/reconciler` passes and `make verify` passes.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/reconciler/adapters/jira/acli_subprocess.py","reason":"no replay of a non-zero create"},{"path":"src/rebar/reconciler/adapters/jira/acli_cli_ops.py","reason":"identity label at create"},{"path":"src/rebar/reconciler/adapters/jira/acli.py","reason":"forward labels to the create"},{"path":"src/rebar/reconciler/create_route.py","reason":"identity label in the create payload"},{"path":"tests/unit/reconciler/test_cloud_create_single_attempt.py","reason":"dropped-response regression test"},{"path":"tests/unit/reconciler/orchestrate/test_leaves_effect_matrix.py","reason":"exact create payload now includes the label"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","managed_refs":[["relates_to","b342-c10c-14b4-4185"],["relates_to","eb07-47d5-f8f5-49f3"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"5706334e-e464-41e0-bb08-5355a705f922","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["bridge"],"ticket_id":"7bed-62ad-fbc3-462f","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Outbound create for sweating-revolting-oriole left an orphan Jira issue (REB-7141) that the reconciler re-imported as a duplicate ticket","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["26d03eee-cfeb-4da3-bd32-10f55454f8dc","4ac385fc-b873-40af-9298-9cf2b37ed5e0","e86c3644-7909-463b-9146-74f6bbcd2b39","91b10df9-c3b5-431a-9922-9760d8c446e9","f43d9a49-46e8-4b94-a5e2-f043d6ea4c27","a9c59674-dadc-4857-9f97-70b63b45fd21","5706334e-e464-41e0-bb08-5355a705f922","6f08a4e9-d14d-4dc9-9b13-d61be7309c1c","b037b575-04b0-44d8-9533-f50f0581f214","3784b317-0a6b-4bf0-9547-8b9ca15cfb14","dcef71f7-450a-4a84-9e6c-471922341a04","7c27c9a8-8527-4dfa-83e4-55fd11fc4d99","79a73976-2287-40fd-8e1a-e7e057b532ac","902e9526-5bda-4e27-b0fd-89b69e2605ac","c93cb577-8c1a-4d39-8304-698881521a6e"]},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1795095603960580281,"uuid":"266cba14-8687-4c78-8886-10ec6ce6710f"}
